## Start here

1. For direction, read [the masterplan](.backlog/masterplan/MASTERPLAN.md).
   For daily progress, open [the workplan](WORKPLAN.md).
2. To change status or record evidence, update Backlog first, then regenerate
   the workplan. Run `backlog instructions overview` and inspect the relevant task.
3. Before creating, executing or finalizing a task, read the matching Backlog
   guide named by the overview.
4. Keep changes within the approved task. Record unrelated discoveries as
   proposed follow-up work instead of expanding scope silently.

The agent responsible for the records refreshes the shared view after each batch
of changes and checks it before handoff. From the project root:

```sh
ruby scripts/workplan.rb --write
ruby scripts/workplan.rb --check
```

Readers just open the Markdown file. Never hand-edit its rows. If the helper
reports a conflicting edit, preserve it and reconcile with the author first.

