## Backlog CLI boundaries

- Run commands from this project root with `BACKLOG_CWD` explicitly set to its
  absolute path. Confirm `backlog config get projectName` before mutations.
- Use the CLI for tasks, drafts, documents and milestones; never hand-edit their
  Markdown files.
- A decision body is the sole direct-edit exception: run
  `backlog decision create`, then fill Context, Decision and Consequences in the
  generated decision file because the CLI has no content-update command.
- `backlog task edit` cannot target a task under `.backlog/completed/`. Do not
  move completed task files by hand during normal work; report a correction that
  requires archival maintenance.
- Let Backlog manage filenames. Link to the existing record path after a rename.

## Writing records for the workplan

Use an action or outcome as the title. Use the board's agreed statuses and
dependency IDs. Keep unapproved ideas in drafts, a proposal status or under the
`proposal` label until explicitly approved; do not promote them just for this view.
In the description use `Effort:` for an estimate in active person-hours (ranges
welcome, never calendar duration) and `Waiting for:` for a pending decision,
input or approval and who can supply it, if known. Remove resolved waits through
the CLI. With no estimate the view says “Not estimated yet”. In implementation
notes or the final summary put `Verified:` on a line with the actual check and
observed result, including limits or failures. Keep supporting detail on the
record. A planned test, a checked box or a completion status alone is not evidence.

